<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Ho, Larry

<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> flat model means that the dictionary
	pointers are a full 32 bits

<[mdc] M.CHRISTOPH2> i means that you have up to 4 gig of
	memory, no segmentation

<[Len] NMORGENSTERN> Thanx

<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> not any of this segmented stuff like F-PC
	uses

<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> well not really 4 gig Mike

<[mdc] M.CHRISTOPH2> why?

<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> there is a problem with standards over 1 Meg

<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> in fact, on a IBM machine, you have a
	problem after 640K

<[Dennis] D.RUFFER> because that is where they put the video and
	other drivers

